      "Language": "ukr",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Heart syndrome features associated with pain, the structure of myocardial ischemia and heart rate derangement were studied in patients with ischemic heart disease (IHD) and concomitant biliary dyskinesia (BD). It was established that BD considerably aggravates clinical course of IHD: increase in frequency of pain and painless episodes of myocardial ischemia in patients with stable exertional angina I-II functional classes by NYHA and single supraventricular and ventricular extrasystoles."},
